Speculative decoding basics: autoregressive generation bottleneck sequential decoding: each token requires forward pass through large target model, memory-bound, low utilization. Speculative decoding uses smaller/faster draft model to generate K candidate tokens sequentially (or block) then target model verifies all K in one forward pass (or parallel) using causal attention over prefix + candidates. If accepted, append tokens; if rejected at position i, sample replacement from target distribution at that position (or modified distribution) and continue. This reduces number of target forward passes from K to ~1 per block, but adds draft passes.

